cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "OEIS A354427 has no other terms below 10^11"
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: "Ellena Godoy"
    given-names: "Jorge"
abstract: >-
  The primes p <= 10^11 for which there are primes q, r with q | p+1,
  r | q^2+q+1 and p | r^2+r+1 (OEIS A354427) are exactly 3, 13, 19, 631,
  1794067711 and 10855016833. So a(5) = 1794067711, a(6) = 10855016833, and
  there is no a(7) below 10^11; the previous search bound was 2^24. Includes
  the reduction lemma that decides each pair (p, q) with one division, the
  full search log, and a dependency-free verifier.
keywords:
  - number theory
  - arithmetic functions
  - computational number theory
  - sum of divisors
  - OEIS A354427
  - De Koninck problem
